mipsgot_nostub_el.so, mipsgot_nostub_n64el.so -- MIPS PIC shared objects
whose imports have no .MIPS.stubs lazy stub, so their global GOT slots hold 0
until the dynamic linker binds them (GH-904;
kuna-cli/tests/mips_got_nostub.rs).

What they are
  Built from mipsgot_nostub.c with -nostdlib. puts is address-taken
  (say_ptr = puts), so the linker gives it no stub and st_value 0; hook is
  a weak reference, also st_value 0. user calls both through their GOT
  slots and guards the hook call with `if (hook)`.
  mipsgot_nostub_el.so    o32 little-endian
  mipsgot_nostub_n64el.so n64 little-endian (mips64r2; load with
                          --target MIPS:LE:64:default)

Why they are vendored
  CI has no MIPS toolchain.

Where they came from
  Ubuntu mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc 10.3.0, GNU ld 2.38 (host):

      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -EL -mabi=32 -O2 -fPIC -shared -nostdlib \
          -Wl,--build-id=none mipsgot_nostub.c -o mipsgot_nostub_el.so
      mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -EL -mabi=64 -march=mips64r2 -O2 -fPIC -shared \
          -nostdlib -Wl,--build-id=none mipsgot_nostub.c \
          -o mipsgot_nostub_n64el.so

  sha256:
    03e0d83a323d7a11a10b16aaa44e18d7f66571cfe597c9b970ebf457e343c17d  mipsgot_nostub_el.so
    577eb0a2310cbf43216b4f344edb1526e51a8f8950bd68bf44323a02a26509df  mipsgot_nostub_n64el.so
